Third-party code
----------------
No third-party code is vendored. The module `src/hashtrinity/` is a port, by the
author, of the author's own `hashtrinity` crate, relicensed here under the terms
of this repository. The revision `4cc14471` named in source comments is the commit of the author's
unpublished `fold` repository that the port started from; it does not resolve in this repository.

GGUF and ggml formats
---------------------
The files below are Rust implementations of the GGUF container and ggml quant
block formats. They were written against llama.cpp (github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp,
rev ece963f41) and its PrismML fork (github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp, rev
9ca265a57) as the format reference, and parts follow that reference's layouts and
arithmetic. Both carry the MIT licence reproduced below, which applies to those
portions.

  src/format/gguf.rs           GGUF reader (llama.cpp ggml/src/gguf.cpp)
  src/format/mod.rs            GGUF container and ggml block unpacking
  src/format/quant.rs          ggml quant block geometry and dequantization
                               (ggml/src/ggml-quants.c)
  src/engine/dequant_lowbit.rs Q1_0, Q2_0, PQ2_0, TQ1_0, TQ2_0, PTQ1_0 block
                               layouts (PrismML fork ggml-common.h, ggml-quants.c)
  src/gpu/decode/pack.rs       Q4 nibble spread (ggml-cuda/vecdotq.cuh)
  src/learn/gguf.rs            GGUF v3 writer (gguf-py/gguf/gguf_writer.py)
  src/learn/imatrix.rs         importance-matrix reader (tools/imatrix,
                               common/imatrix-loader.cpp)
  src/learn/seal.rs            Q4_K block fit (ggml-quants.c quantize_row_q4_K_impl)

